  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Below normal temperatures continue for the \nfirst half of the week before warming takes hold towards middle \nto end of this week. \n\nHigh pressure over the Midwest will build east and will be over\nthe Ohio and western Appalachians on Tuesday, then will meander\nover the Mid-Atlantic starting on Wednesday and through the end\nof the week.\n\nWith clear skies and light winds tonight, radiational cooling \nconditions will allow temperatures to drop into the upper 20s \nfor most of the area, except in the low 30s in Delmarva, and in \nthe mid 30s in/around Philadelphia. Lows will be in the upper \n30s along the coasts owed to the warmer ocean waters.\n\nTemperatures will moderate as the week progresses with highs\ngetting into the 60s by Friday.",
